The issue was that FastAPI's `request_params_to_args` function in `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py` was indiscriminately adding all received header keys to the `params_to_process` dictionary, even those containing underscores, when `convert_underscores=True` (the default). This allowed Pydantic to validate and accept underscore-containing headers by matching them to the field names, bypassing the intended restriction that only hyphenated headers should be accepted.

To resolve this, the second loop in `request_params_to_args` should be modified to skip header keys containing underscores if `convert_underscores` is enabled and the key was not already processed (i.e., not explicitly allowed).

